oy this herbal tea.\n4. Most people who dislike coffee will enjoy this herbal tea." 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209477 1072 #uuid "e37fcf3b-d183-5a49-a529-63a6e07979af" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208107 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209478 1069 "q-309594" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209478 1071 "Dataset $P$: $5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5$\n\nDataset $Q$: $2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5$\n\nTwo datasets, $P$ and $Q$, are given above. Which of the following statements about the means and medians of the datasets is true?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209478 1072 #uuid "8e08291f-1f92-50d8-9599-afca5d8743d7" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209479 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208113 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209479 1069 "q-309596" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209479 1071 "A city council surveyed $250$ households to learn whether they were satisfied with the recycling services. Every household in the sample responded, and $82%$ indicated that they were satisfied. Based on this information, which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n1. Of all households in the city, $82%$ would say they are satisfied with the recycling services.\n2. If another random sample of $250$ households were surveyed, exactly $82%$ would say they are satisfied.\n3. The true proportion of satisfied households in the city is approximately $82%$." 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209479 1072 #uuid "c699deb2-f3ef-547b-bfdc-83ce7f042242" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209480 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208119 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209480 1069 "q-311002" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209480 1071 "A survey was conducted using a random sample of biology instructors from community colleges in Texas. The instructors surveyed were asked about the laboratory manuals they currently use. What is the larges