2186045585 true] [17592186209490 1069 "q-317435" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209490 1071 "At a science fair, there are $500$ attendees in the venue. Each attendee is in exactly one of three zones: Robotics, Chemistry, or Astronomy. If an attendee is selected at random, the probability they are in Robotics is $0.26$, and the probability they are in Chemistry is $0.47$. How many attendees are in the Astronomy zone?There are\n{{field-1}} attendees in the Astronomy zone." 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209490 1072 #uuid "3717fc1b-4afe-5f88-8c56-b79740da5411" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209491 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208180 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209491 1069 "q-317687" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209491 1071 "In a school club membership report, the counts of members by club and gender are shown in the table below.\n\n|  | Male | Female | Totals |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Robotics Club | $44$ | $46$ | $90$ |\n| Debate Club | $27$ | $33$ | $60$ |\n| Art Club | $31$ | $39$ | $70$ |\n| Environmental Club | $78$ | $42$ | $120$ |\n| Totals | $180$ | $160$ | $340$ |\n\nWhich club has a male count that is closest to $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the total number of males in the report?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209491 1072 #uuid "cd07e1b0-45c1-538d-87e2-4890a06b5946" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209492 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208186 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209492 1069 "q-317874" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209492 1071 "At a farmers’ market, the counts of shoppers by stall type and time of day are shown in the table below.\n\n|  | Morning | Afternoon | Totals |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Produce | $45$ | $27$ | $72$ |\n| Bakery | $56$ | $25$ | $81$ |\n| Dairy | $33$ | $46$ | $79$ |\n| Flowers | $66$ | $41$ | $107$ |\n| Totals | $200$ | $139$ | $339$ |\n\nWhich stall type has a Morning count that is closest to $\\frac{1}{4}$