5585 true] [17592186209496 1069 "q-321350" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209496 1071 "Triangles $△MNO$ and $△XYZ$ are plotted in the $xy$-plane. Triangle $△MNO$ has vertices $M$, $N$, and $O$ at $(3, 4)$, $(3, 8)$, and $(7, 4)$, respectively. Triangle $△XYZ$ has vertices $X$, $Y$, and $Z$ at $(3, 4)$, $(3, 4 + 4k)$, and $(3 + 4k, 4)$, respectively, where $k$ is a positive constant. If $m∠N = v^{∘} + 35^{∘}$, what is the measure of $∠Y$?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209496 1072 #uuid "2eaa0415-dc2b-53bd-a40d-5a153d2248bd" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209497 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208211 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209497 1069 "q-321354" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209497 1071 "Triangles $△ABC$ and $△DEF$ are plotted in the $xy$-plane. Triangle $△ABC$ has vertices $A$, $B$, and $C$ at $(3,-1)$, $(3, 2)$, and $(7,-1)$, respectively. Triangle $△DEF$ has vertices $D$, $E$, and $F$ at $(3,-1)$, $(3,-1 + 3k)$, and $(3 + 4k,-1)$, respectively, where $k$ is a positive constant. If $m∠B = t^{∘} - 5^{∘}$, what is the measure of $∠E$?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209497 1072 #uuid "94e4e424-e675-5caf-9af8-ca1b6885c779" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209498 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208217 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209498 1069 "q-322640" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209498 1071 "Which of the following expressions is equivalent to\n$\\frac{\\sin 18^{∘}}{\\sin 72^{∘}}$?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209498 1072 #uuid "d1d8368b-ee80-5a08-b1a7-fd776f4f1258" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209499 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208223 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209499 1069 "q-322646" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209499 1071 "Which of the following expressions is equivalent to\n\n$(\\sin 18^{∘})(\\cos 72^{∘}) + (\\cos 18^{∘})(\\sin 72^{∘})$?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209499 1072 #uuid "963b05e3-053c-54e9-be64-891b4c88b0d5" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209500 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208229 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209500 1069 "q-323591" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209500 1071 "![](images/d6/d69e86adda83350f8fe94e650e840ec51e6464e9345cf8e53981b0f2dab1bb14.png)\n\nDuring the first part of a study, a marble was rolled off a $10$-inch-high table. The graph below shows the height $y$, in inches, of the marble $x$ seconds after it left the table.\n\nDuring the second part of the study, the marble was rolled the same way, but from a table that is $4$ inches taller than the first table. Which of the following graphs could represent the height $y$, in inches, of the marble $x$ seconds after it left the table during the second part of the study?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209500 1072 #uuid "8a9dab3b-05e2-5b4e-9720-07ee9bb68774" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209501 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208235 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209501 1069 "q-324204" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209501 1071 "The side lengths of right triangle $ABC$ are given as $AB = 60$, $BC = 80$, and $CA = 100$. Triangle $ABC$ is similar to triangle $PQR$, where $B$ corresponds to $Q$ and $C$ corresponds to $R$. What is the value of $\\sin R$?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209501 1072 #uuid "3cecfd45-0465-596e-b855-ca9aa6458145" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209502 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208241 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209502 1069 "q-324252" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209502 1071 "In the equation $y = gx^{2} - 3h$, where $g$ and $h$ are positive constants, how many times does its graph intersect the graph of $y =-7h$ in the $xy$-plane?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209502 1072 #uuid "ce26e7a8-5383-543c-bf17-a7a3a140a071" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209503 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208247 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209503 1069 "q-325379" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209503 1071 "A sports team wants to estimate the average amount of money each fan spends on food and drinks during a game.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Randomly selecting fans from the ticket sales database and contacting them for the amount they spent.\n2. Surveying fans seated in the front row during the game.\n3. Asking people leaving through the VIP lounge." 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209503 1072 #uuid "24ebaccf-a038-59ba-8cac-2e4aa9680a49" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209504 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208253 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209504 1069 "q-325385" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209504 1071 "A city council wants to estimate the average amount of time residents spend commuting to work each day.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Posting a survey on the city’s website and asking visitors to respond.\n2. Randomly selecting residents from the city census database and contacting them to ask about their commute times.\n3. Asking for responses from people who call into a local radio show about traffic." 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209504 1072 #uuid "2dbd169c-b003-53cd-a10a-544a66980f79" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209505 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208259 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209505 1069 "q-325400" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209505 1071 "At a coffee shop, $2,400$ customers made purchases last Saturday. The manager randomly reviewed receipts from $80$ customers and found that $12$ of those customers purchased a pastry. Which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion?" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209505 1072 #uuid "4b1ef9be-6fb9-5100-bcb7-1820737807bc" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209506 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208265 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209506 1069 "q-325423" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209506 1071 "A university surveyed $750$ students who were selected at random from its campus and asked, “Do you plan to attend the spring sports festival this year?” Of those surveyed, $62%$ responded “no.”\n\nBased on this result, which of the following conclusions are appropriate?\n\n1. Of all students at the university, exactly $62%$ do not plan to attend the spring sports festival this year.\n2. If another $750$ students selected at random from the university were surveyed, the proportion who say “no” is likely to be close to $62%$.\n3. If $750$ students selected at random from a different university were surveyed, the proportion who say “no” is likely to be close to $62%$." 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209506 1072 #uuid "2fd11e96-d7da-5867-b30c-e0cc38dc1d3c" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209507 1068 #edb/ref 17592186208271 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209507 1069 "q-325424" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209507 1071 "A health department surveyed $1,000$ residents who were selected at random from a small city and asked, “Have you received a flu vaccine in the past year?” Of those surveyed, $40%$ responded “yes”.\n\nBased on this result, which of the following conclusions are appropriate?\n\n1. Of all residents in the city, approximately $40%$ have received a flu vaccine in the past year.\n2. If another $1,000$ residents selected at random from the city were surveyed, the proportion who say “yes” is likely to be close to $40%$.\n3. If $1,000$ residents selected at random from a different city were surveyed, the proportion who say “yes” is likely to be close to $40%$." 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [17592186209507 1072 #uuid "4b754e28-6015-5723-8fb0-15f7da784930" 13194139533376 17592186045585 true] [1759218620950